values.content:
Analyze this support ticket for escalation risk.

Ticket: {{ $json.ticketId }}
Customer: {{ $json.customerName }}{{ $json.accountTier ? ' (' + $json.accountTier + ')' : '' }}
Account MRR: {{ $json.mrr ? $json.currency + $json.mrr : 'unknown' }}
Account age: {{ $json.accountAge ? $json.accountAge + ' days' : 'unknown' }}
Previous tickets: {{ $json.previousTicketCount }}
Product area: {{ $json.productArea || 'not specified' }}

Message thread:
{{ $json.messageThread.map(m => '[' + m.role.toUpperCase() + (m.timestamp ? ' ' + m.timestamp : '') + '] ' + m.content).join('\n\n') }}

Return JSON:
{"escalation_risk":"none|low|medium|high|critical","escalation_signals":["specific signals detected that indicate risk"],"churn_risk":"none|low|medium|high","churn_signals":["specific churn indicators if any"],"sentiment":"calm|frustrated|angry|hostile","root_issue":"what the customer actually needs resolved (may differ from what they asked)","recommended_action":"one of: standard_response|prioritize|assign_senior|escalate_to_manager|immediate_call|account_review","escalation_rationale":"why this action level was chosen","suggested_response_opener":"first 2 sentences the agent should write — empathetic, specific to what they said, not generic","internal_note":"what support management should know about this ticket"}
